\* TIER-2 CERT LEG — baseline safety. EXPECT: clean, and it MUST reach FIXPOINT.
\*
\* Acceptance criterion (PROJECT_STATE §6): this leg is one of the two baselines that
\* must reach a CONCLUSIVE verdict inside the time-box. "Conclusive" for this leg means
\* TLC prints `Model checking completed. No error` — a time-box exit is INCONCLUSIVE and
\* certifies nothing (rule 16).
\*
\* Bounds are IDENTICAL across all six cert legs; the ONLY difference between this file
\* and the four mutation legs is the mutation switch. That is what makes a mutation fire
\* here provably mutation-induced rather than bound-induced (the Mut3Fast/BaselineSafetyFast
\* pairing principle, generalized to the whole cert set).
\*
\* @MAXMSGS@ is substituted by the tlc-cert workflow from the `cert_msgs` dispatch input.
\*
\* MaxCkpt: the cert legs use 2, the standing large-bound configs use 3 — both inside the ratified
\* 2–3 range (F-UNBOUNDED-SEGMENT, §7.21). 2 is the value the core module's own justification calls
\* sufficient for every SHAPE of prepare/commit/drop/crash interleaving; 3 adds a second succession
\* without a new shape. The cert legs must DRAIN inside the time-box, and an independent counter
\* multiplies the space, so they take the smaller sufficient value; the standing configs are
\* depth-bounded evidence with no drain obligation and take the larger.
\* This is not bound-shopping: the §6 acceptance criterion is SELF-POLICING — all four mutations
\* must still FIRE at the certified bounds, so a MaxCkpt too small to exhibit the harm makes a
\* mutation go silent and DISQUALIFIES the bound rather than passing it.
SPECIFICATION Spec

SYMMETRY Sym

CONSTRAINT
CertConstraint

CONSTANTS
Stages = {s1, s2}
MaxEpoch = 1
MaxRId = 1
MaxAttempt = 2
MaxPos = 1
MaxCrashes = 1
MaxCkpt = 2
MaxMsgs = @MAXMSGS@
EnableUnservable = TRUE
ResetTruncates = TRUE
AttemptFencing = TRUE
AbortGuardEnabled = TRUE

INVARIANTS
Inv
